V919 Vibration Motor Projects Overview

This folder contains a collection of basic V919 Vibration Motor projects created to explore and understand the fundamentals of reading and processing button inputs using an ESP32.
Each project focuses on a different method of detecting button presses and responding to user input, helping build a strong foundation before moving on to more advanced
electronics, sensors, and interactive embedded systems projects.

These examples demonstrate concepts such as  . They also serve as reference implementations that can
be reused in future robotics, IoT, and embedded system projects.

